    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Battles of Tarain (1191, 1192) led to the establishment of the Delhi Sultanate under Muhammad Ghori.",
        "Babur defeated Ibrahim Lodi in the First Battle of Panipat (1526), laying the foundation of the Mughal Empire.",
        "The Battle of Plassey (1757) marked the beginning of British political rule in Bengal through diplomatic intrigue.",
        "The Battle of Buxar (1764) firmly consolidated British military supremacy in North India.",
        "The Treaty of Allahabad (1765) granted the East India Company the Diwani rights of Bengal, Bihar, and Orissa."
      ],
